---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const cv = `${base}cv/`;
---
<BaseLayout title="About — GeoSmart" description="About Camila Fernández — geology undergraduate, geoscience communicator and aspiring subsurface geologist.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-kicker">The geologist behind GeoSmart</div>
      <h1>Curious about<br />what lies beneath.</h1>
      <p class="muted">A geology student building a path towards subsurface and offshore geoscience.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page">
    <div class="container profile">
      <div class="profile-photo">
        <span>Your field photo<br />goes here.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="section-kicker">Hi, I'm Camila.</p>
        <h2>I like geology because it is part science, part detective work.</h2>
        <p>I'm a geology undergraduate at the Universidad Complutense de Madrid, currently spending the 2026–27 academic year at NTNU in Trondheim. I'm particularly interested in the subsurface: how geological history, physical properties and geophysical data come together to help us understand what we cannot see directly.</p>
        <p>My interests sit at the intersection of <strong>subsurface geology, geophysics, sedimentology and energy resources</strong>, with a growing focus on seismic interpretation and geological reservoirs.</p>

        <h2>Where I want to go</h2>
        <p>I'm working towards a career in <strong>offshore and North Sea geoscience</strong>, especially exploration and subsurface work. I want to keep developing the technical skills needed to interpret geological and geophysical data while understanding the bigger geological story behind them.</p>
        <p>For me, good geoscience is not only about getting an interpretation right. It's also about being able to explain <em>why</em> it makes sense.</p>

        <h2>What I'm building</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Subsurface &amp; offshore geology</strong> — geological reasoning below the surface and in energy-related settings.</li>
          <li><strong>Geophysics</strong> — seismic interpretation and using geophysical evidence to understand structures.</li>
          <li><strong>Sedimentology</strong> — depositional environments, sedimentary records and reservoir thinking.</li>
          <li><strong>GIS &amp; geological mapping</strong> — turning spatial data into useful geological information.</li>
          <li><strong>Scientific communication</strong> — making geological ideas understandable without making them less rigorous.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Academic path</h2>
        <div class="timeline-mini">
          <p><strong>Universidad Complutense de Madrid</strong><br /><span>Geology · 2021–present</span></p>
          <p><strong>NTNU, Trondheim</strong><br /><span>Erasmus exchange · 2026–27</span></p>
        </div>

        <h2>Beyond the degree</h2>
        <p>I'm also interested in the space between science and people. Through science outreach and <strong>@_geomila_</strong>, I enjoy sharing geology in a way that feels curious, visual and approachable. GeoSmart brings those two sides together: the technical work I'm learning to do and the stories that make geology worth looking at in the first place.</p>

        <div class="about-links">
          <a class="btn" href={cv}>See my CV →</a>
          <a class="text-link dark" href="mailto:c.fernandez@geosmart.es">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
